> a(x: u32, y: u32) = (x*x) xor (y*y) xor 5
> b(x: u32, y: u32) = (y*y) xor (x*x) xor 5
> equiv a b
a and b are equal on the domain of a (proved by SAT: 9280 AIG nodes, 0 conflicts)
> c(x: u32, y: u32) = (x*x) xor (y*y)
> d(x: u32, y: u32) = (x*x) + (y*y)
> equiv c d
c and d differ at 65453 points of the sample, e.g. x=1, y=1: 0 vs 2
